CORE
main.cpp
--cpp17
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
^.*does not uniquely resolve.*$
--
Verifies that the implicit default constructor of a class derived
from two specializations of the same template can be type-checked
without hitting the spurious "symbol 'X' does not uniquely resolve"
diagnostic.  `full_member_initialization` synthesises a base-class
member-initializer whose `cpp_namet` is the unqualified base
`base_name`; when two bases share the same `base_name` (e.g.,
both are specializations of the same template) the resolve in
`typecheck_member_initializer` would otherwise return both
candidates.  The fix scopes the resolve to the specific base
subobject's struct via the `#base_type` codet attribute set by
`full_member_initialization`.
